{
  "name": "cuttlefish",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/cuttlefish.py; base: the octopus): a common cuttlefish, the mantle 30 cm, 45 cm with its arms -- a CEPHALOPOD, not a fish: a broad FLATTENED OVAL MANTLE (the cuttlebone inside), a narrow FIN SKIRT running its whole length along each side (one membrane sheet a side); a short head with big eyes bulging either side and the siphon under it; EIGHT SHORT ARMS held together in a cone in front, each a tapering tube with SUCKERS (the coat pattern `suckers`) on its own waving bone (arm0-7), and two longer pale TENTACLES running out under them to flattened, suckered CLUBS (tentacleL/R); the pupil should be W-SHAPED -- the engine's eyes have round | bar | slit only, so it is `bar`; the male's ZEBRA display, pale bands across the mantle's back and the arms, along the fin's base, over a MOTTLED brown (`mottle`). A SWIMMER (the fish's plumbing: `fly`), the arms waving out of step.",
